From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tejun Heo <htejun@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:02:26 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] scx_lavd: Fix the autopilot configuration binding

sys_stat.bpf.c defines is_autopilot_on weak next to the strong definition in
util.bpf.c. Both survive the link: BTF keeps the weak variable and the ELF
symbol resolves to the strong one, at different offsets in .rodata. The Rust
skeleton writes the BTF offset and the update_sys_stat() relocation reads
the ELF symbol, a byte nothing ever writes.

So the autopilot flag the BPF side tests is never set: in the default
autopilot mode do_autopilot() never runs and lavd stays in its initial power
mode under any load. Remove the weak definition so both sides refer to the
one in util.bpf.c.

Fixes: 8964cb0356d2 ("[RFC] scx_lavd: initial refactor for separate unit compilation")
---
 scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/sys_stat.bpf.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/sys_stat.bpf.c b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/sys_stat.bpf.c
index 6466ec5b1..cc3d97ad3 100644
--- a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/sys_stat.bpf.c
+++ b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/sys_stat.bpf.c
@@ -27,7 +27,6 @@ extern const volatile u64	slice_min_ns;
 extern const volatile u64	slice_max_ns;
 extern volatile bool		__weak no_core_compaction;
 extern volatile bool		__weak reinit_cpumask_for_performance;
-const volatile bool	__weak is_autopilot_on;
 
 int do_autopilot(void);
 u32 calc_avg32(u32 old_val, u32 new_val);
